+# Carbon accounting & Quantum connector runbook (PoC)
+
+Overview
+- This document explains how to use the newly added carbon accounting and quantum connector scaffolds.
+
+Carbon accounting (per-job)
+- Requirements:
+  - Prometheus scraping DCGM exporter with a power metric (dcgm_gpu_power_draw_watts or similar)
+  - PROMETHEUS_URL env var pointing to Prometheus server
+  - Optional CARBON_API_URL + CARBON_API_KEY for carbon intensity API (ElectricityMap or cloud provider)
+
+- Flow:
+  1. Worker calls start_meter(job_id, pod_name, node_name, gpu_index) at job start.
+  2. Worker calls stop_meter(job_id, region) at job end.
+  3. stop_meter will call energy_accountant.compute_energy_kwh to integrate power samples and compute kWh.
+  4. stop_meter will call carbon_lookup to compute gCO2e/kWh and compute co2e_kg.
+  5. Billing uploader will attach energy_kwh and co2e_kg to charge record and attempt to post it.
+
+- Acceptance test:
+  - Run a sample job instrumented with start/stop meter; verify evidence file in /tmp/aegis_job_meters/<job_id>.json contains energy_kwh and co2e_kg.
+
+Quantum connector (PoC)
+- Components:
+  - services/quantum/connector.py : high-level connector
+  - services/quantum/simulator_adapter.py : uses Qiskit if available, else mock
+  - services/agents/tool_adapter_quantum.py : tool adapter used by orchestrator
+
+- Flow:
+  1. Orchestrator submits a tool step that references tool "quantum" with a circuit payload.
+  2. Orchestrator worker calls tool_adapter_quantum.run_tool_quantum which invokes connector.
+  3. Connector returns evidence dict which the orchestrator worker stores with per-step evidence.
+
+- Next steps to productionize:
+  - Implement provider-specific adapters (AWS Braket, IBM, Azure)
+  - Add provider credential management, quota accounting, and billing hooks
+  - Capture provider calibration metadata and noise model for reproducibility
+
